WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:07.230
We will now begin the lottery for the 
Ouka Festival locations and timetables.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.200
We will call your name in the order 
you submitted your paperwork,

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.990
so when we do, please come up to the stage.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.320
First, the choir club.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.790
Here!

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.720
Okay, Shiori-chan, go up there for us.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.020
Huh? You want me to?

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.210
Yep. Go ahead.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.790
R-Right.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.920
Everyone's so focused.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:33.000
This is going to be a great school fair.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.230
The choir club gets Auditorium 1 at 1 P.M.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:46.770
Good.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.980
"Choir club"...

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:52.290
Next, we have the street performing society.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:52.990
Right here!

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.490
The street performing society 
gets Auditorium 2 at 10 A.M.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.240
We have the drama club next.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.620
H-Here!

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:09.380
<b>Club Timetable Lottery</b>

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:09.380
The drama club gets Auditorium 1 at 3 P.M.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.410
Thank you.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.030
Good job, Moeka!

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.730
Next, the arts and crafts club.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:21.400
The arts and crafts club gets 
Auditorium 1 at 3:30 P.M.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.550
<b>Art</b>

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:29.260
<b>Kendo Club

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.270
That was nerve-wracking.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:31.640
Nagiko-chan, you go.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:33.660
You always have good luck 
with this kind of thing.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.400
Okay?

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.880
Haruka, you do it.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.280
You're the vocalist.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.760
Try getting the grand prize!

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.820
Huh? Me?

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.830
There's only the grand prize or the 
first slot in the morning left.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:47.780
<b>Auditorium 1</b>

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.460
<b>Time</b>

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.830
The slot in the morning would suck.
I couldn't wake up in time.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.840
Next is Neuron Cream Soft 
from the light music club.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:55.720
I-It's our turn!

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:56.890
Haruka.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.780
Huh? Should I?

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.840
Do it!

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.280
Let's go!

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.710
Okay...

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:09.060
Please give it a turn.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:34.960
A-14.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.520
Auditorium 1 at 4:30.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.240
We did it!

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:18.010
<b>Evolutionary Girl</b>

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:16.480
This is a big responsibility.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.110
It's right before the bonfire.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.400
Yeah, we need to get the crowd hyped.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.640
So, what should our set list be?

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.500
We need a new song.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:29.420
I want to do one.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.040
Me, too!

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.340
So, you're going to write 
the song, right, Nagiko-chan?

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.220
That's fine.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:39.340
As long as Haruka writes the lyrics.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:44.360
Okay, then I'll make the 
costumes with Momoko-chan.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:45.930
What kind should we make?

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:48.300
Studs and zippers.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.470
We stick them all over and rock out!

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:53.810
It'd be too heavy to move in...

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.980
What do you two want to wear?

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:00.800
Something cute would be nice.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.390
Something fluffy with frills?

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:06.860
How about a miniskirt like idols wear, then?

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:08.960
What? Really?

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.880
It'd look great on you, Nagiko-chan.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.490
No, it wouldn't.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:17.050
That means Momoko-chan and 
Kurumi-chan will work on costumes,

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.620
but what about you, Sumire-chan?

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:20.710
I'll think on how to decorate the costumes.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:21.370
Sure.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.920
And Nagiko-chan's writing the song?

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:27.260
And the lyrics are coming 
from Haruka, of course.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.740
Yeah...

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:30.140
I'll do my best.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:37.080
So by majority vote, Class 2-A will 
be doing a shogun tea house.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.890
<b>Shogun Tea House   Maid Cafe   Eating Contest</b>

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:38.300
<b>Shogun Tea House  Maid Cafe  Eating Contest</b>

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.310
All right!

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.640
<b>Shogun Tea House</b>

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:41.510
The girls will dress as town girls and handmaidens.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:44.550
The boys will dress as samurai or ninjas.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.030
Yes!

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:52.450
Huh?

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:55.450
That's a lot.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:57.460
What's that?

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:03.710
I have the proposals for what each class 
and club wants to do for the festival.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.350
I see.

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:08.450
And we're going to check them.

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:12.080
We need to see if they're 
appropriate for Seiou Academy.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:14.800
Oh, that sounds like a lot of work.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:15.360
Do your—

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:16.600
We'll <i>all</i> do our best.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:23.060
We received a request to extend the 
school closing time until 10 P.M.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:26.110
I'm in favor, but we should implement 
it three days before the event.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:29.270
I think it's a little early to do that now.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:32.430
Everyone's working hard.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:35.870
I'm sure we can rest easy 
and enjoy the Ouka Festival.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:43.740
I'm a young husband.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.320
How's that sound?

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.010
Why a period piece?

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:50.590
The Edo period has been on my mind lately...

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.120
Yo.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.430
Getting anywhere?

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.640
Not yet...

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:56.140
I'm sorry.

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:57.890
Um...

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:02.790
Is it okay if I start thinking 
about the costumes later?

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:06.760
I'd like to match them with the new song.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.400
I'll do what I can...

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.480
I need another day...

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:13.240
No, two or three days.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.660
You can't write something good if you rush.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.660
We still have time.

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:21.100
Y-Yeah, that's true.

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:25.200
White Clouds

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:25.200
It's a shogun tea house!  Neuron Newton

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:25.200
Evolution??

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:25.200
Straight-cut bangs

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:25.200
Reflected in the window glass

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.210
<b>Welcome to the 
Arts and Crafts Club</b>

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:28.500
I'm thinking of making the theme

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:30.380
for our cosplay fashion show a carnival.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.510
We'll have a high-tempo song,

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:35.300
and maybe a little dancing added in, too.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:40.110
So someone from the broadcast committee 
can choose the song and be the MC, right?

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:42.450
Yeah. Think they'll do it?

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.560
What about the models?

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:47.180
No need to worry about that.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:50.570
I have a talented scoutwoman 
handling that for us.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:54.450
Hey, you over there.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:58.760
Have you ever wanted to
 discover hidden parts of yourself?

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:01.620
Wh-What is this about, Mochizuki-san?

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.000
You get to wear pretty clothes,

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.290
and get pretty pictures taken.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.630
Everything about it is wonderful!

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:13.510
Mochizuki-san, you're not asking for
ridiculous favors again, are you?

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.520
I'm not.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:17.870
Right?

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:18.900
Yeah!

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.440
Fumio-chan, do you want to enter, too?

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:22.770
It's the arts and crafts club's show.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:27.450
I'm sorry, but I have an exhibit for the library.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.040
That's too bad.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.280
Come and check out our show.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.650
Sure.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:39.700
<b>Shogun Tea House</b>

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.700
Ta-da!

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:42.080
Look at this.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:44.470
They're handmaidens!

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:45.750
Handmaiden sisters!

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:49.230
Shiranui-san and Kazemachi-san look great, too.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:51.260
Come on in, you two.

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:56.280
They're cute!

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.370
I'm used to wearing kimonos,

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:04.560
but it feels weird wearing something so fancy.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.690
Yeah, this wig is so heavy,

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.600
it's making me dizzy.

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:11.610
We're going to have a line out the door!

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:15.840
Is Kazemachi-san from 2-A and 
the light music club here?

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:16.700
Yes?

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:18.570
<b>Student Council Room</b>

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:21.110
About the Neuron Cream Soft performance...

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:23.330
We need a summary of your performance

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:25.440
or we can't allow you to participate.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:28.040
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:30.210
We haven't decided for sure yet...

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.710
This is a problem.

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:38.090
I'd like to report everything 
to the school by next Monday.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:41.350
The student council needs to
 check over the documents,

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:44.250
so ideally, we'd like it by tomorrow morning, but...

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:48.780
Can't we do something for them,

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:50.980
Risa-chan, Mutsumi-chan?

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:56.840
Very well.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:59.280
Let's give them until 5 P.M. on Friday.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.980
That's the latest we can go.

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:04.240
Um, if we don't make it in time...

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:06.500
You won't be able to perform.

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:12.530
Girl Friend BETA.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:16.010
What? Really?!

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.300
Yeah...

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:19.160
We only have until the end of the week.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:23.620
We're also at fault for leaving 
this all to you, Haruka.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:24.770
Yeah.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:26.790
I'll do my best.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:28.800
I mean, I want to.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:32.060
I hope I can, anyway...

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:34.140
Haruka-chan-senpai!

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:37.080
Is there anything I can help you with?

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.240
Help me?

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.920
I don't know...

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:42.880
Oh!

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:46.720
I mean, if you can help, it'd be great...

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:50.120
But I'm just not sure what you could do.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.340
Yeah.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:57.110
Do you have any ideas for the lyrics?

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:57.760
Huh?

00:10:58.280 --> 00:10:59.800
Well...

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:06.180
I'd like to write a song that everyone can 
get into, and that I can enjoy singing.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:10.700
Like something about how it's 
important to have dreams,

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:14.650
or something to cheer up 
people who are having trouble.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.940
Maybe something about friends or family,

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:20.210
or something about being grateful 
to everyone around you?

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:23.770
The future of Japan, or Earth's environment?

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:25.840
Love and peace...

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:26.950
Stuff like that...

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:30.210
Is all of that going to fit in one song?

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:30.960
Oh...

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:32.700
What about you, Haruka?

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:33.590
Huh?

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:36.130
What do you want to sing?

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.300
I...

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:40.520
I, um...

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.440
I don't know.

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:43.340
She's completely lost.

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:46.650
You're not singing because you have to.

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:48.600
Why not relax a bit?

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:50.300
But...

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:53.350
We get to be the last act on the stage...

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:58.940
Haruka-chan, here's the sheet 
music I was borrowing...

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:00.760
What's wrong?

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.950
Shiori-chan!

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.950
Seiou, fight! Fight! Fight!

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:09.080
You can't come up with lyrics?

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:10.510
Yeah...

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:12.250
You're always singing.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.640
Why not just do it like that?

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:17.240
I'm always singing?

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:18.210
Huh?

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:23.130
You know, like, "the new croquette buns 
at the school store are yummy."

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:26.720
Or, "there are some flowers
 I don't know in the courtyard."

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:30.660
Yeah, she did sing that.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:31.770
I remember now.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:34.600
I like the one that goes...

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:37.360
"I don't understand this Sei Shonagon person.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:40.650
I'm just tired at dawn."

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:45.780
I want to hear a song that reminds 
me of Haruka-chan like that.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.180
That's it.

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:50.770
Let other people worry about 
world peace and love for all mankind,

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:53.240
and just sing about everyday stuff.

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:54.660
Everyday stuff...

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:56.040
I know!

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.410
Let's go find stuff!

00:12:57.410 --> 00:12:59.080
Huh? Find stuff?

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:00.280
Where?

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:02.820
The school!

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:05.210
I bet there are tons of ideas around here.

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:07.360
Is that okay?

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:08.520
It's fine.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.440
A little to the right.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:11.990
This way?

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:12.760
Yeah.

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:17.190
Kazemachi-dono?

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:18.970
You came at just the right time.

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:21.040
Huh?

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:27.900
We're having trouble deciding what 
we should serve at the tea house.

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:30.480
Red bean jelly is simple and delicious!

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:35.540
It's even used in rations. Japanese sweets 
that we can be proud of on a global scale!

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:37.040
Right...

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.800
A tea house needs rice dumplings!

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.440
I'm not letting this go!

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:41.800
What do you think, Yukawa?!

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:55.870
I think they're both equally good.

00:13:57.150 --> 00:14:00.670
We're asking which one suits a tea house better.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:02.330
I think they're both good.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:04.340
Can't you just serve both?

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:06.860
We could do that!

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.820
But I still say red bean jelly is best, 
and I stand by that!

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:11.160
What do you mean, "best"?

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.330
Best means best!

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:12.670
Kazemachi-dono.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:13.330
Hm?

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:17.410
I'm looking forward to the
light music club's performance.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:19.460
Y-Yeah.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:20.860
Thanks.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:25.920
<b>Welcome to the
 Arts & Crafts Club</b>

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:24.330
Perfect timing.

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:25.920
Could you put this on?

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.550
Please don't move.

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:30.990
What's this about?

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:32.660
Just temporarily sewing this on.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.310
We didn't have enough mannequins.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.520
Thanks for helping.

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:40.850
By the way, are the costumes for 
Neuron Cream Soft going well?

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:45.090
Uh... Anytime now. Right?

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:46.760
Y-Yeah.

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:49.740
All the extras,

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:54.160
I want you all to run around like 
there's a big robot over there.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.950
A big robot?

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:57.410
I don't want to run.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:00.220
We need someone who gets 
crushed, too, if you prefer that.

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:01.290
I want that <i>less</i>.

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:04.280
Come on, please?

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:07.600
I'll go see your concert as thanks.

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:14.120
I'm used to using a bow,

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:16.560
but I don't have any experience with horses.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.020
I hope this works.

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:21.140
I just need to practice, I guess.

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:26.560
I'm sure the light music club band 
is under a lot of pressure, too.

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:29.030
Y-Yeah.

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:37.090
People expect a lot from us.

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:39.570
I'm happy, but it's a lot of pressure.

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:42.040
We need to do the best we can.

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:45.910
It'd be nice if it wouldn't start yet.

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:46.720
Huh?

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:48.880
Oh... I didn't mean it that way.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.320
Once the culture festival starts,

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:53.640
all that's left is for it to end.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.810
I was just thinking it'd be nice

00:15:55.810 --> 00:16:00.590
if we could keep having fun getting 
fired up, like we are now.

00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:02.490
I know what you mean, Haruka-chan.

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:04.750
I was thinking the same thing.

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:08.780
I bet a lot of girls are thinking the same thing!

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:12.690
Why not make that our song?

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:13.530
Huh?

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.560
I'm not sure if I can...

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.910
But I'd like to sing about that!

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:37.510
Darjeeling really is the king of teas.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.840
<b>Staff   Student Council</b>

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:39.850
Don't you think?

00:16:39.030 --> 00:16:39.840
<b>Approved</b>

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:41.560
Sure, sure.

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:51.090
Is the light music club still not ready?

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:54.190
It's almost the deadline.

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:56.010
The rules are the rules.

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:57.700
We need to enforce them.

00:16:58.340 --> 00:16:59.970
Yeah...

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:01.790
I guess we have to.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.450
I-I'm sorry!

00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:16.740
That's all we need.

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:18.010
Good luck.

00:17:19.590 --> 00:17:21.390
Haruka-chan-senpai!

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:34.770
The 51st Annual
 Ouka Festival

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:40.160
<b>Fortunes</b>

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:36.350
Come on over...

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:37.580
...and have a look!

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:40.650
We have the fortune teller of the century.

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:44.120
Check out Ouka Z-chan, the robot
that the robotics society developed!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.910
She'll dance for you!

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:49.670
Manga Research

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:49.670
It's the best issue the manga research 
society has published since its creation!

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:53.670
<b>Great Chemistry Experiment</b>

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:53.670
If we add the mysterious reagent that I developed...

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:57.600
I think I just heard something...

00:17:57.600 --> 00:17:59.330
Huh? Heard what?

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:00.970
Nothing, never mind.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:05.850
Menu 

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:05.850
Welcome!

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.780
Come along and drop in!

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:13.130
You two are about to perform, right?

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:14.660
You can go.

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:15.600
Thank you!

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:18.530
Thanks. We'll leave the rest to you!

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:23.240
<b>Light Music Club 
Neuron Cream Soft 
Performing at 4:30

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:35.880
Sorry for the wait!

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:37.420
Yo!

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.650
We'll never finish.

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:42.040
No helping it now.

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:44.010
We'll just go on in our gym clothes.

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:45.230
What?

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:48.730
We can't give up, Nagiko-chan-senpai!

00:18:49.050 --> 00:18:50.580
Sh-She's right.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:51.560
We have to try.

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:55.070
No, let's take a reality check here.

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:59.320
Do you really think we can 
finish all this in two hours?

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:04.080
It's all because I thought up these costumes...

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.540
Don't feel bad!

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.640
You tried your best.

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:09.410
Actually, you tried too hard.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:16.710
Wait here for a bit!

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.970
Hey! Where are you going?!

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:37.900
Spasibo, Kokomi-san!

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:40.370
You're a true étoile!

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:42.970
An étoile?

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:46.410
A wonderful dancer, an étoile!

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:48.760
A star.

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:50.160
Yulia-san...

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:53.170
You think too highly of me.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:58.960
I got a lot of good shots!

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:04.720
Sounds like they're done.

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:07.100
Let's go over everything one last time.

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:08.860
Yeah!

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:11.600
Is Tokitani-senpai here?!

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:13.340
What's wrong?

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:15.370
You're completely out of breath.

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:19.110
Tokitani-senpai, I need to ask a favor.

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:21.920
A favor?

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:29.490
You want us to finish these 
outfits in one and a half hours?

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:33.500
This looks like it'd take three more days...

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:44.760
Let's make this happen.

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.890
P-President!

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:49.880
Kurumi-chan!

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:51.470
Thank goodness!

00:20:51.470 --> 00:20:55.980
<b>Light Music Club</b>

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:54.120
Let's get started, Nae.

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:55.980
R-Right!

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.090
Oh, Romeo!

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:03.490
Wherefore art thou Romeo?

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:09.530
A girl's dreams and hopes.

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:11.340
Romantic dresses.

00:21:11.340 --> 00:21:13.910
The title is "Afternoon Dress"!

00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:40.150
Neuron, we can't wait any longer!

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:43.340
All right, we got it!

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:44.320
I'm so tired...

00:21:43.340 --> 00:21:44.320
Sorry for taking so long.

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:46.860
Thank you, Tokitani-senpai!

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:48.610
Let's go.

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:50.030
Yeah!

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:01.170
Neuron!

00:22:03.100 --> 00:22:05.300
Cream Soft!

00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:10.830
Sorry for the wait, everyone!

00:22:10.830 --> 00:22:12.560
Are you ready to have fun?

00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:14.800
Here we go!

00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:17.810
We're Neuron Cream Soft with "Evolutionary Girl"!

00:22:21.050 --> 00:22:22.520
Do what you want to do.

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:24.220
Just be yourself.

00:22:24.220 --> 00:22:27.040
Going beyond your limit is just right.

00:22:27.040 --> 00:22:29.770
Go beyond evolution, Evolutionary Girl.

00:22:29.770 --> 00:22:32.340
Shake it off and start running up.

00:22:32.340 --> 00:22:33.740
The sky's the limit!

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:24.760
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:10.770 --> 00:24:12.460
3, 2, 1, go!

00:24:12.460 --> 00:24:13.790
Tomo Oshii here!

00:24:13.790 --> 00:24:15.530
I'm normally working in the background,

00:24:15.530 --> 00:24:17.080
but next time I'll be stepping out a bu... a bit...

00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:17.910
One more time!

00:24:17.910 --> 00:24:18.990
I can't!

00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:20.390
It'll be fine!

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:24.760
<b>Episode 10: Princess & Pride</b>

00:24:20.390 --> 00:24:22.990
Next time: Princess & Pride.

00:24:22.990 --> 00:24:24.160
On air!
